{"event": "tool_call", "time": 1793241045.001541, "run_id": "1e76378398284a21a47f0ccb83b47c5c", "seq": 28, "tool": "write_note", "arguments": {"title": "DeepInfer config/formatter/stats-queue mechanisms", "content": "environ.py: EnvVar[T] is a non-data descriptor with __slots__=('name','init','lock'); __set_name__ registers into _descriptors[name]; __get__ takes self.lock, checks owner.__dict__.get(self.name,self); if cached is not self returns it; else calls self.init(os.getenv(self.name)), wraps exceptions as type(e)(f'{self.name}: {e}') (falling back to bare raise on TypeError), then setattr(owner,self.name,value) so value is cached in class dict. Factory methods: int(default), float, bool, str, str_or_none (lambda v: v), int_or_none (int(v) if v is not None else None), choice. rearm(name) does setattr(envs,name,_descriptors[name]); rearm_all() loops _descriptors and setattrs each. So new config DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS should be a factory method validating int>='32'. logger.py: _setup_logger sets root level DEBUG, creates _default_handler StreamHandler(sys.stdout) once (if None), level INFO, adds handler; then builds NewLineFormatter(_FORMAT, datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT, use_color=sys.stdout.isatty()) and setFormatter on existing handler; root.propagate=False. init_logger(name) gets logger, DEBUG, propagate True for deepinfer/prefix, else attach _default_handler if not present. stats_logger.py: from deepinfer.logger import init_logger; logger = init_logger(__name__); _log_worker(q) iterates iter(q.get,None), optional sleep by rank, for m in msgs: logger.info(m), need_sleep=q.empty(), exceptions traceback.print_exc(). _emit_logs puts msgs onto _log_queue. Only change: logger.info(m, extra={'keep_full_message': True}).", "evidence_ids": ["ev-8554ade850ecb397d235", "ev-246c6e73a88cb2c9edc3", "ev-ef45633e339c9e5fd82f", "ev-d69c220908cefeeae7f2", "ev-51e2fa3b9fc1aebe86f3", "ev-ddb5be78a5cf6218d616", "ev-c8859274b7c70879ff16", "ev-5a3c8c1ca1246b61b813", "ev-5abfdabfb9